    Incident Summary — Service Disruptions (2024-12-01)
    
    Overview:
    On 2024-12-01 we experienced a brief disruption affecting multiple backend services following a recent infrastructure change. Three components 
experienced partial outages; all were recovered by the on-call team.
    
    Key figures:
    - Total Downtime: 50 minutes (sum of recorded component downtimes)
    - Number of Affected Users: 1,800 (sum of reported affected users)
    - Root Cause: Post-deployment resource and integration issues manifested as:
      - Auth Service: Database connection pool exhaustion
      - Search API: Redis cache eviction failure
      - Notifications: Unexpected rate limit from third-party API
    
    Timeline (UTC):
    - 2024-12-01T10:00:00Z — Auth Service outage begins; downtime 25 minutes; 800 users affected
    - 2024-12-01T10:45:00Z — Search API outage begins; downtime 15 minutes; 600 users affected
    - 2024-12-01T11:30:00Z — Notifications outage begins; downtime 10 minutes; 400 users affected
    
    Impact:
    - Brief interruptions to authentication, search, and notifications functionality for a subset of users.
    
    Immediate mitigation and current status:
    - On-call team restored service availability; services were recorded as restored in the incident logs.
    - Current status: Services operational.
    
    Planned follow-ups:
    - Conduct a post-incident review focused on the recent infrastructure change and deployment process.
    - Re-evaluate DB connection pooling and monitoring for the Auth Service.
    - Review Redis eviction policy and capacity for the Search API.
    - Coordinate with the third-party provider to address rate-limiting and implement robust backoff/retry logic for Notifications.
    - Enhance monitoring and alerts for resource exhaustion and cache pressure.
    
    External communications guidance (per Huang):
    - For external partners, avoid citing exact downtime or user counts. Instead, describe the event as a "brief disruption" and emphasize the corrective 
measures and improvements implemented to prevent recurrence.
    
    Prepared by: Internal Communications (automated draft)
    

  kind: "FileEditorAction"

