    Incident Summary — External Partners (2024-12-01)
    
    Overview:
    On 1 December 2024 we experienced a brief disruption to several backend services following a recent infrastructure deployment. Authentication, search, 
and notification functionality were intermittently affected for a subset of users. Our on-call team restored full service availability quickly.
    
    Root cause (high-level):
    Post-deployment resource and integration issues surfaced after the infrastructure change. Contributing factors included database connection pooling 
under-provisioning, cache eviction behavior under load, and interactions with third-party rate limits.
    
    Impact (summary):
    - Short-lived interruptions to authentication, search, and notification services for a subset of users.
    - No customer data loss detected.
    - Services fully restored; operations are stable.
    
    Actions taken and planned improvements:
    - Immediate: on-call team restored services and applied mitigations to stabilize capacity and retries.
    - Short-term: increased monitoring and alerts for resource exhaustion and cache pressure; adjusted connection-pool sizing and retry/backoff logic.
    - Medium-term: post-incident review of the deployment process, strengthened deployment validation and capacity testing, and coordination with 
third-party providers to avoid similar rate-limiting issues.
    
    Commitment:
    We are focused on preventing recurrence and will share outcomes and timelines from the post-incident review with partners as appropriate.
    
    Contact:
    For partner questions, please coordinate with your account or partner manager.
    

  kind: "FileEditorAction"

